-- MediChain — Phase 0: tenancy, identity, configuration, audit.
--
-- Generated by `prisma migrate diff` from prisma/schema.prisma, then extended
-- by hand with the constraints Prisma's schema language cannot express
-- (partial unique indexes) and the extension the schema depends on (citext).
--
-- Never edit a migration after it has been applied to any environment. A
-- migration is a record of what happened, not a description of what should be
-- true — editing one makes two environments that report the same migration
-- history hold different schemas, which is the hardest kind of drift to find.
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

-- `citext` backs `user.email`, so that `Admin@Example.com` and
-- `admin@example.com` cannot both register. The comparison is case-insensitive
-- in the database rather than in application code, which means it also holds for
-- a query issued by a script, a migration, or a support tool.
--
-- `pgcrypto` is NOT required: `gen_random_uuid()` has been built into Postgres
-- since 13, and this project targets 17.
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS "citext";

